  "notes": "{溜|た}まる is a godan verb meaning to accumulate, collect, or pile up over time.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {溜|た}める (transitive: to save up, accumulate)\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- お{金|かね}が{溜|た}まる: money accumulates\n- {疲|つか}れが{溜|た}まる: fatigue builds up\n- ストレスが{溜|た}まる: stress builds up\n- {仕事|しごと}が{溜|た}まる: work piles up\n- {埃|ほこり}が{溜|た}まる: dust collects\n- {水|みず}が{溜|た}まる: water pools/collects\n\nNUANCE:\nOften implies gradual, unintentional accumulation, and frequently has a negative connotation (stress, work, fatigue piling up).",
